{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Who…</b> The word מתברך is not like ונברכו בו (Genesis 18:18), for there is a difference between them." "And the sense of <b>by the God of amen</b> is that all the world will recognize that there is no true god besides Him, for amen is from the root of אמונה (Isaiah 25:1), and it is an epithet of the Name, and the meaning is that one acknowledges that this is true, or prays that he desires it to be true." "And the sense of <b>for [the former troubles] are forgotten</b>: the troubles that came upon the righteous, the servants of HaShem, are hidden, for when the wicked saw that troubles came upon them, they would mock them and their service."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 65, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:03.603804333Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}